          "Count the days rather than counting on the new year. The window closes 31 days after the sale, so a loss taken in the second half of December is not clear until some point in late January. Waiting for 1 January clears nothing, and a repurchase on 2 January is the mistake this whole exercise exists to avoid. Pushing the repurchase past the end of January puts you comfortably clear of anything sold in December.",
          "A quieter benefit of picking replacement holdings you have not touched all year is that it also sidesteps the 30-days-**before** half of the rule, which is the half people forget. If you have not bought it recently, there is nothing behind you to collide with."
