          "**Being out of your strategy for a month is a real cost.** This is the part that gets left out of the tax framing entirely. For 31 days you are holding something you did not choose for its returns, which means you are exposed to whatever the market does and your strategy does not get to respond. In a month that moves sharply, that cost can be larger than the tax it saved. The harvest is worth doing when you have gains to offset and the numbers justify it, not automatically.",
