          "**K-1 funds are taxed on a different basis.** Many of the leveraged, inverse and commodity products that appear in Composer strategies are partnerships rather than ordinary funds, and their tax treatment does not resemble a share sale. That is a reason to know which of your holdings issue a K-1 before you plan around any of this, not a reason to assume the rule does or does not reach them."
